{
  "hitlcad": 2,
  "name": "nas-case",
  "backend": "build123d",
  "brief": {
    "title": "Compact 3D-printed micro-ATX NAS case, 4 × 3.5\" HDD",
    "summary": "Dual-chamber case for a micro-ATX board, 4 × 3.5\" drives, an ATX PSU and two reused 120 mm fans, split into pieces that each fit a 256 × 256 mm bed and print in PETG without supports. Front and rear shells (panel + floor + ceiling) are joined at the middle with M3 screws into heat-set inserts. A separate motherboard tray spans both shells and ties them together, and four flat side panels close it. The fans push air front-to-back through the drive cage.",
    "key_dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Motherboard (micro-ATX)",
        "value": 244,
        "note": "244 × 244 mm, on 6.35 mm brass M3 standoffs"
      },
      {
        "name": "Clearance above PCB",
        "value": 80,
        "note": "low-profile CPU cooler (≤ ~70 mm) and low-profile cards"
      },
      {
        "name": "Wall",
        "value": 3,
        "note": "PETG"
      },
      {
        "name": "Fan size",
        "value": 120,
        "note": "2 × 120 × 25 mm, 105 mm hole spacing"
      },
      {
        "name": "Cable room in front of the board",
        "value": 35,
        "note": "for forward-facing SATA ports"
      },
      {
        "name": "Printer bed",
        "value": 256,
        "note": "every piece ≤ 254 mm as it prints"
      }
    ],
    "features": [
      "9 printed pieces from 8 parts: front_shell, rear_shell, divider (motherboard tray), hdd_rail_left, hdd_rail_right, side_front (placed left and right), side_left_rear, side_right_rear; each modelled the way it prints",
      "All seams use M3 screws into ruthex M3 × 4 heat-set inserts (Ø4.0 × 5 mm holes); bosses have 40° undersides and horizontal holes are teardrops, so nothing needs support",
      "Seam: socket-head screws from counterbores in the front shell's bosses into the rear shell's; side panels: countersunk screws, flush; divider and rails: button-head screws up through the floor and down through the ceiling",
      "Front: 120 mm intake fan with printed grille, power-button hole. Rear: 120 mm exhaust fan, I/O aperture, 4 low-profile slots, ATX PSU opening + ledge",
      "Top vents over the PSU, side vents over the CPU",
      "The motherboard sits on eight 6.35 mm brass standoffs screwed into heat-set inserts in the divider"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Fans are 120 × 25 mm (regular PC fans; 105 mm between screw holes)",
      "The PSU is a standard ATX unit (150 × 86 × 140 mm)",
      "Low-profile CPU cooler and low-profile PCIe cards only",
      "Standoff positions are approximate micro-ATX positions; check them against the real board before printing",
      "The board's SATA ports face forward, so 35 mm of cable room is left in front of the board",
      "Screw heads under the floor and on the ceiling stand 1.65 mm proud: the case stands on them or on stick-on feet"
    ],
    "open_questions": [
      "Do your board's SATA ports face forward or up? If up, board_front_gap can drop to ~5 mm and the case gets 30 mm shorter",
      "CPU cooler height?",
      "PSU mounting screws: add the four ATX holes once the PSU is confirmed",
      "Drive screws: the Ø3.5 holes in the rails are a tight fit for 6-32 UNC screws (Ø3.51); widen them if the screws do not pass"
    ]
  },
